{:adr-id "2627100000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-5221 (service activities incidental to land transportation) land-transport-support-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607121000" "ADR-2607152500" "ADR-2607121200"]
 :mirrors "cloud-itonami-isic-3512 (energy.* module shape, verified sibling actor)"

 :context
 "ISIC Rev.5 5221 = service activities incidental to land transportation:
  toll-road/highway operation, bus-terminal operation, and related
  infrastructure-support services -- NOT the carriage of passengers/freight
  itself (that is cloud-itonami-isic-4911/4912/4920) and NOT third-party
  inspection consulting. Live registry.edn :name for \"5221\" independently
  verified fresh: \"Service activities incidental to land transportation\",
  unambiguous, matching siblings 5222 [water], 5223 [air], 5224 [cargo
  handling], 5229 [other], each its own registry entry. UNUSUAL premise
  versus most entries in this ADR series: `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/
  cloud-itonami-isic-5221` confirmed a PRE-EXISTING repo, not a 404 --
  already at :blueprint tier (CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md/CONTRIBUTING.md/
  GOVERNANCE.md/LICENSE/README.md/SECURITY.md/blueprint.edn/docs/ only, no
  deps.edn/src/test) from an earlier bulk-scaffolding pass. This work ADDED
  the missing implementation on top of that existing boilerplate rather
  than re-scaffolding a fresh repo. The reference sibling actors named in
  this task (cloud-itonami-isic-4911/4912) were ALSO found to still be
  blueprint-tier-only at investigation time (no deps.edn/src/test either),
  so this build instead mirrored cloud-itonami-isic-3512's verified
  Store/Advisor/Governor/Phase/Operation/Sim module shape module-for-module
  -- confirmed by direct inspection of the tarball actually implemented and
  green, not assumed. Toll-road/bridge/parking-facility structural-safety
  and traffic-safety decisions warrant the standard governor pattern even
  though this is an infrastructure-support actor, not a carrier: any op
  finalizing an infrastructure-safety-clearance decision must be a hard,
  permanent block, and any 'flag a concern' op must always escalate, never
  auto-commit-eligible."

 :self-trip-fix
 "Known bug class this fleet has repeatedly hit: bare-noun scope-exclusion
  terms (e.g. 'safety', 'structural') self-match inside the mock advisor's
  own legitimate default rationale text, self-blocking the actor's happy
  path -- especially acute here since :flag-structural-safety-concern's
  entire purpose is to talk ABOUT a structural/traffic-safety concern using
  exactly those bare-ish words. Fix: scope-exclusion terms
  (`landsupport.governor/finalization-phrases`) phrased as the
  finalization/execution ACTION ('finalize the structural-safety
  clearance', 'certify ... structurally safe', JA '構造安全性クリアランスを確定'),
  never a bare noun, applied to ALL FOUR allowlisted ops' proposal text
  regardless of which op it claims to be. Verified by a dedicated
  regression test suite
  (test/landsupport/scope_exclusion_test.clj:default-mock-advisor-
  proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion and
  flag-structural-safety-concern-specifically-never-self-trips) asserting
  all 4 default proposal generators, for a clean registered+verified
  facility, never trip :structural-safety-clearance-finalization and never
  HARD-hold."

 :decision
 "Fill in cloud-itonami-isic-5221 (pre-existing blueprint repo) with
  Store/Advisor/Governor/Phase/Operation/Sim, mirroring
  cloud-itonami-isic-3512's energy.* module shape module-for-module as
  landsupport.*:
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore + DatomicStore (langchain.db-backed),
    string-keyed facilities directory
    (facility-id/facility-name/facility-type/registered?/verified?/
    structural-safety-concern-unresolved?/jurisdiction), append-only
    ledger + per-op append-only logs (facility-record/maintenance-schedule/
    concern/supply-order)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + mock-advisor + llm-advisor seam, 4 ops all
    :effect :propose -- log-facility-record, schedule-facility-maintenance,
    flag-structural-safety-concern, coordinate-supply-order
  - Governor (Land Transport Support Governor): 4 named HARD checks
    (facility-unverified, closed op-allowlist, effect-not-propose,
    structural-safety-clearance-finalization scope-exclusion) +
    always-escalate-ops #{:flag-structural-safety-concern} + high-cost
    (>$50000) escalation gate for coordinate-supply-order,
    confidence-floor 0.6
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout (phase1 = log-facility-record only, approval;
    phase2 += schedule-facility-maintenance/coordinate-supply-order,
    approval; phase3 auto-commits log-facility-record + (governor-gated)
    coordinate-supply-order when clean+confident;
    flag-structural-safety-concern never auto, any phase)
  - Operation: real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->
    decide->commit|hold|request-approval), interrupt-before
    #{:request-approval}, NOT a stub -- mirrors energy.operation exactly
  - Sim: clojure -M:dev:run demo, full happy path + always-escalate flow +
    all HARD-hold scenarios (unregistered facility, unverified facility,
    out-of-allowlist op, structural-safety-clearance-finalization attempt)
  - Tests: governor_test, scope_exclusion_test (dedicated self-trip
    regression), phase_test, store_contract_test, operation_test -- 40
    tests / 138 assertions green
  - All .cljc portable, no JVM-only interop. AGPL-3.0-or-later. Existing
    README/GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/blueprint.edn
    boilerplate kept as-is; README extended with an 'Implementation (R0)'
    section describing the actual actor module"

